      "message": "Fixed in PS16. The driver reads `show running-config interfaces \u003cport\u003e` before configuring; for a non-100G speed it issues `no speed` (when a speed statement exists) and `no error-correction encoding reed-solomon` (when RS-FEC is present) before the forced token. Raising to 100G clears a stale forced speed before `speed auto 100g-2`. Both `no` forms are gated on the running config as suggested. Tests pin the 100G-\u003e25G and 25G-\u003e100G sequences. A 0/unset speed is still left untouched (no target to program).",
